NNAAMMEE
     newgrp - change to a new group

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     nneewwggrrpp _g_r_o_u_p

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     nneewwggrrpp changes the caller's group identification to _g_r_o_u_p
     and starts a new shell, /bbiinn/sshh, under that group id.
     Access is checked against the entry for _g_r_o_u_p in /eettcc/ggrroouupp:
     membership is granted if the caller's login name appears in
     the group's member list, if the group has no password and no
     member list, or, failing that, if the caller supplies the
     group's password correctly.  A member name prefixed with !
     in the member list is instead explicitly denied access.

     On success, nneewwggrrpp sets its real and effective group id to
     that of _g_r_o_u_p and its real and effective user id back to the
     caller's own user id, then execs /bbiinn/sshh as a login shell.
     On failure it prints a short message and execs an ordinary
     /bbiinn/sshh without changing group.

